2 CONT When Jon Tallaksson's father died in 1522, he inherited the entire Aukland farm, which  was valued at 2 1/2 laupar butter. He is named in the tax lists of 1519 and 1521. In 1521, Jon had to pay 22 marks 3 shillings, as well as 26 
2 CONC lodd silver and 4 marks 2 shillings in tax. This shows that he was a very rich man. Jon is also named in the probate document of 1522 detailing the division of his father's estate. That document still exists and is preserved at th
2 CONC e Aukland farm. He is last named in 1565 and probably died shortly thereafter.
2 CONT
