1 OCCU Hovmästarinna för blivande drottning Margareta, Kone til Ridder Knut
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Märta Ulfsdotter Hjortufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Ulf Gudmarsson (Ulvåsa) and Heliga Birgitta Birgersdotter 
2 CONT * Birth:	1320 in Ulvaas, Östergotlands, Sweden
2 CONT * Marta was a Swedish court lady. As a court mistress, she was responsible for Queen Margaret's upbringing and teaching.
2 CONT * Death:	circa 1371 in exile in Norway.
2 CONT *  [http://wadbring.com/historia/sidor/birgitta.htm '''Märta was read in Anteckningar om Svenska Quinnor ca 1886:'''] "Märtha Hjorthufvud was the daughter of Nerike's lawyer Ulf Gudmarsson Hjorthufvud and S: ta Brigitta, was born 
2 CONC around 1320 and married for the first time to Sigvid Ribbing. After Ribbing's death married Knut Algotsson . the Nordic Semiramis), she raised this and her own daughter Ingegerd (who later became the first abbess in Wadstena) so s
2 CONC trictly according to the old way, that the rice was thereby diligently used. History tells us that she maintained such superiority over her royal pupil that, even after she became queen of Norway, she had to submit to the same cru
2 CONC de punishment ".
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://books.google.com/books?id=8nbUjE7AsQYC&pg=PA371&lpg=PA371&dq=Sigurd+Erlingsson+Ribbing&source=bl&ots=LJf2rHeJEI&sig=ACfU3U0cWteNZbilMREEbENWgoJVG9fL3g&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiTt6_jg9DpAhWSu54KHTvABT8Q6AEwGnoECAM
2 CONC QAQ#v=onepage&q=Sigurd%20Erlingsson%20Ribbing&f=false '''Sigvid Ribbing, i Skane,'''] Sigvid Ribbing married Märta Ulfsdotter Hjorthufvud in 1341 in på Ulfåsa herrgård i Östergötland.  Märta married Sigvard Ribbing in 1337 - "the 
2 CONC wedding at Ulvåsa" (the wedding march of the same name was composed by August Söderman much later). Mother Birgitta opposed the marriage because she disliked Sigvard Ribbing. The couple settled at Vapnö Castle outside Halmstad in 
2 CONC Halland. Märta became a court mistress and supervisor for Margareta Valdemarsdotter, when she as queen and wife of Håkan (Håkon) VI arrived in Norway and Akershus. Märta had a daughter, Ingegerd, who was raised together with Queen
2 CONC  Margareta Valdemarsdotter. Ingegerd became an adult abbess in Vadstena monastery, but was removed from office, accused of forgery, embezzlement and frivolous conduct. Märta was also married to the knight Knut Algotsson. Daughter 
2 CONC of Ulf Gudmarsson Hjortufvud eller Folkunge & Brigitta Brigersdotter eller Santca Brita  who had also married to the knight Knut Algotsson (lion, Bengt Algotsson's family ). 
2 CONT * Married (2) After the death of her first husband in 1345, she married '''Knut Algotsson''' (Bengt Hafridsson's family) .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Sigvid Ribbing, i Skane=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peter Sigvidsson Ribbing,''' (dead in 1379), commonly called Peter Ribbing, is mentioned among King Albrek's followers in the stagnation treaty with King Magnus's followers in 1371. He became the Council of Ministers in 13
2 CONC 75 or 1376, made the 1379 pilgrimage to the Holy Land, wrote his will in Rome and died on his way home in Florence shortly after he became a knight. Married to Marshal Karl Ulfssons by Tofta half sister Kristina Ulfsdotter ( Sparr
2 CONC e av Tofta ) but died childless after inheriting her half brother Arvid Ribbing in Uppland drowned son Arvid Ribbing
2 CONT * 2. '''Arvid Sigvidsson Ribbing''' son of Sigvid Ribbing,  at Arms; Lived in 1390. - Married 1st with Ingeborg Magnusdotter, of old Stureätten, in her 2nd marriage; daughter of the Knights and the Council of Magnus Magnus Amundss
2 CONC on  (Sture) and widow of Ulf Nilsson, à Vapn, of whom she was given the morning gift of Hamneryd and Sundra farm and qvarn, but with whom she had no children: - 2: o with Brita Pehrsdotter; daughter of the Knight Pehr Sture. 
2 CONT * 3. '''Bengt Sigvidsson Ribbing,'''  lived in 1409.
2 CONT * 4.  '''Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter,''' birth circa, 1360, lived in 1409. Married Peter Andersson Prika (stjärna), son of Anders Prika i Gällstad.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Knut Algotsson av Bengt Hafridssons ätt=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingegerd Knutsdotter,''' born 1356, died 1412; abbess in Vadstena Monastery 1388-1403. Ingegerd Knutsdotter was the daughter of Märtha (Margareta) Ulfsdotter and Knut Algotsson, and the maternal grandchild of Saint Bridget of
2 CONC  Sweden. She was raised with the future Union Queen Margaret, as her mother served as royal governess. She was inducted into the Vadstena Abbey in 1374 at the age of eighteen, the same year as the body of Bridget was returned to S
2 CONC weden.
2 CONT * '''Katarina Knutsdotter,''' died about 1412, court mistress at Filippa of England 1412
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Knutsdotter,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://poulkryger.dk/p2b0e3fb1.html Sigvid "The Robber" Bengtsson Ribbing]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in 1295 as Seved Knutsson, was courtier over Halland and lord of the castle to Falkenberg. Ribbing married in 1337 with Märta Ulfsdotter (Ulvåsaätten), daughter of Saint Birgitta. The marriage has been named Bröllopet på
2 CONC  Ulvåsa by posterity. died about 1350. Lives in Vapnö castle, Halmstad. From the family Ribbing no. 15. Sigvid was born in the early 14th century. Through an inheritance in 1340, he received the estate Vapnö in Halland. (Vapnö has
2 CONC  belonged to the Ribbing family since the beginning of the 14th century). Sigvid was a courtier over southern Halland between the years 1330 and 1345. He is described as a cruel and hard man. Stayed in Norway and Sweden in 1335. S
2 CONC igvid married Märta Ulfsdotter in 1341. She was the daughter of Ulf Gudmarsson Hjorthufvud and Birgitta Birgersdotter (Saint Birgitta). Märta was only 13 years old when it was decided that she would become the wife of Sigvid Ribbi
2 CONC ng. The marriage was more of a "political agreement" between her father and the reigning King Magnus Eriksson than a happy marriage. Sigvid Ribbing who was a "robber" made himself rich through thefts from the ships in the Kattegat
2 CONC  between Denmark and Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus Eriksson wanted power over trade in Sweden and in order to have a calm trade between the countries, he made a well-planned move by letting Councilor Ulf Gudmarsson's daughter Märta marry Sigvid Ribbing and persuade him
2 CONC  to stay calm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through the marriage between Märta and Sigvid, Ulf Gudmarsson also strengthened his position as an adviser to the king because the agreement with Sigvid Ribbing was a political success for King Magnus Eriksson. 
2 CONT Marta's mother, Saint Birgitta, opposed the marriage between Märta and Sigvid. 
2 CONT When Sigvid and Märta got married, Saint Birgitta did not want to attend the wedding at Ulfåsa but sat outside the wedding hall. After a while she regretted it and eventually she went to them in the hall at Ulfåsa. (More about thi
2 CONC s can be read in Magdalena Ribbing's book - The Ribbing 700 years in Sweden's history). 
2 CONT Märta and Sigvid were married for just over 10 years and had four children. 
2 CONT Sigvid Ribbing died in the early 1350s when the Great Depression ravaged Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0375.html '''Von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3, page 371''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigvid Ribbing in Scania;''' Called in Anna Bülow's Notice of Old Family Seved Ribbing; Where a well-born lord of Scania, who lived in 1345, who may have come from Norway in 1335; Referred to as a stern and hard man; Considered
2 CONC  the ancestor of all the Ribbings in Sweden, and with him Peringsköld begins his hand written pedigrees of the Ribbing family. - Married to Märta Ulfsdotter (Hjorthufvud), in her 1st marriage, b. In the year 1320; Was around 1353—
2 CONC 1363 a strict Adulterer for Queen Margaretha in her younger years; † in Norway and 
2 CONT buried there; daughter of Riddaren and Svea Rikes Råd  and Lagmannen i Nerike Ulf Gudmarsson  (Hjorthufvud or Folkunge), to Ulfåsa, who first carried in the weapon a deer head with a neck, then his the mothers or Folkungevapnet, a
2 CONC  lion, with Brigitta Birgersdotter or Sancta Brita (see Brahe, No. 1) and remarried with the Knight Knut Algotsson to Hammarö, of the old Grip- or Griphufvudslägten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peder''', à Vapn; Svea Rikes Råd; Was childless and in 1402 went with his wife to the holy tomb, but they were to die on the road. In 1375, as a pledge, the Second Council of Sweden sometimes confirmed a King Albrecht's Chart
2 CONC er; likewise in 1376 the King's letter to the dioceses in the kingdom stated: shall finally give Hamneryd (two farms in Ås) and Flateryds mill in Wadsbo district, which all he inherited from his nephew Arvid Ribbing, to Wadstena m
2 CONC onastery, according to a written record written in 1518, which Arvid Skeff, who was Ingeborgs, Arvid Ribbing 's wife Redesven, must have given Peder Ribbing is called by Catharina Knutsdotter (Griphufvud), in  his confirmation let
2 CONC ter for Wadstena monastery brother (half-brother). - Married 1360 to Christina Ulfsdotter; daughter of Riddaren, Riks-Råd and Lagmannen Ulfo Abjörnsson (Sparre, No. 7), to Tofta, with his 1st wife, Margaretha Sunesdotter (Bååt, No
2 CONC . 3). 
2 CONT * '''Arvid'''  (son of Sigvid Ribbing, Tab. 2), à Vapn; Lived in 1390. - Married 1st with Ingeborg Magnusdotter, of the old Stureätten, in her 2nd marriage; daughter of the Knight and Riks-Råd Magnus Amundsson (Sture) and widow of
2 CONC  Ulf Nilsson, à Vapn, of whom she received as a morning present Hamneryd and Sundra farm and mill, but with whom she had no children: - 2nd with Brita Pehrsdotter; daughter of the Knight Pehr Sture. Sons: Arvid; Drowned unmarried 
2 CONC in Upland &Peder; Svea Rikes Råd.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg''' Married Peter Andersson Prika, i Möne 
2 CONT * '''Bengt'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Elgenstiern=
2 CONT
2 CONT born 1319 in Ulvåsa, Östergötland, died in 1399. Märta Ulfsdotter was born on Ulvåsa farm in Östergötland. Her father was teammate Ulf Gudmarsson Deer head and the mother was Heliga Birgitta. Märta was their first child. Märta was
2 CONC  first married to Sigvid Ribbing. They married in 1341 at Ulfåsa manor in Östergötland. They were married for over 10 years and had three children together. Sigvid Ribbing died about 1350 in digerd death. Märta remarried the knigh
2 CONC t and the great man Knut Algotsson. He did not agree with the Swedish king Magnus Eriksson. In 1357 Knut Algotsson expelled from Sweden to Norway. During her stay in Norway, Märta became the mistress of Queen Margareta Valdemarsdo
2 CONC tter. (Queen Margareta was born in Denmark in 1353. At the age of 10, Margareta married the 13-year-old Håkon of Norway. Håkon was the son of the Swedish king Magnus Eriksson. Queen Margareta remained in Denmark until 1366 and mov
2 CONC ed to Håkon in Akershus in Norway where Märta raised Queen Margaret). Märta and Ulf's daughter Ingegerd later became abbesses in Vadstena monastery, but were dismissed from the office when she was accused of forgery and embezzleme
2 CONC nt. Märta died in 1399.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Elgenstiern.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Reference Book: Forsand 275=
2 CONT
2 CONT Marta Ulfsdtr Sweden was born circa 1319 at Sweden. She married Sigvid Knutson Ribbing circa 1345. She married Knut Algotsen IX Lejon Folkunge, son of Algot Brynjulfsen Lejon and Kristina Tolvesdtr Sweden, in 1355 at Sweden. She d
2 CONC ied before 1375 at Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Algotsen IX Lejon Folkunge was born before 1330 at Sweden. He married Ingegerd Magnusdtr ? circa 1350. He married Marta Ulfsdtr Sweden, daughter of Ridder Ulf Gudmarsen Ulvåsa and den hellige Birgitta Birgersdtr Finnstad, in 
2 CONC 1355 at Sweden. He lived between 1356 and 1375 at Norway.
2 CONT
