1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Øystein Rian: Bratsberg på 1600-tallet. Stat og samfunn i symbiose og konflikt side 110
2 CONT S. H. Finne-Grønn: Fra Skiens ældste skifteprotokoller [https://www.nb.no/items/a2faa619fe1f8fc9dc8354dac18d3446 Norsk Personalhistorisk Tidsskrift, II.10 (1920)] side 375
2 CONT Skipper, reder, trelasthandler, sagbrugseier. Rådmann, Skien, 1594-1607. Også kjent som Gjert Jansen Hollænder.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Gjert Janssn [Geert Jans] persumably of Harlem (thus noted in norwegian records), is believed to have some connection to a family named Groll. He was a captain and sailed from the Neatherlands to Langesund and from there into Skie
2 CONC n. In 1585 he had cityzenship in Harlem. In 1586 he settled in the city of Skien in Norway and soon became a member of the city council. In 1594 he became city counsillor. Possibly his first wife was named Sarka [Sarke(n)] and he 
2 CONC probably had the following children in his first marriage; Jan, Cato, Dorte (Dorothy) and Karen. In his second marriage with Femja Sørensdotter, the persumed eldest daughter was named Sarke.
