1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Andres av Stovreim=
2 CONT
2 CONT (Andres Simonson av Stovreim)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.nb.no/items/2b815100ded40f38f49176f3ad4017c7?page=91
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Simon Kåreson (Baglerhøvding) and Margareta Arnesdotter Stovreim 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married after the Heim's appearance from Denmark with the '''Gudrun Gregoriusdotter,''' dotter to the Lendmann Gregorius Jonson of Blind Heims Ætta in Sunnmøre
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Gregorius Andresson Stovreim;''' married in the spring of 1242 in Nidaros with the most of Kongsberg, Mrs. Cecile Håkonsdotter, dotter of Håkon Håkonson and Kanga the young.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Ættesambandet_Stårheim_–_Orre_på_Jæren_i_mellomalderen The old Samband Stårheim – Orre at Jæren in the middle age]
2 CONT
2 CONT Andres Simonson Laut As said drunk with King Valdemar hostage to Semja I Tunsberg in 1204. He had halated in Denmark, a godkjende of Valdemar, the peace treaty at Kvitsøy (1208). No, Andres came home and made Tunsbergsysla under h
2 CONC is brother. Andres went ahead and reminded that the townspeople of Tunsberg in 1190 had killed his father at Tristein. He raised his case against the former for the Tunsberg men the gondola, and they crawled fines for their father
2 CONC . Philippus was and son of Simon Kåreson, but had never thought of noko such a sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT He would be opposed to such progress. Andres Laut on it. The townspeople of Tunsberg were very fond of Philippus after this. Andres Simonson married after the Heim's appearance from Denmark with the Gudrun Gregoriusdotter, dotter 
2 CONC to the Lendmann Gregorius Jonson of Blind Heims Ætta in Sunnmøre. Gregorius was the son of Lendmann Jon Hallkellson, who was married to Margreta, Dotter to Harald Gille. Andres arrived in great vein with Skule Bårdson, co-brother 
2 CONC of Inge Bårdson, after his brother Philippus Bagler Royal fall from 1217, and Skule was eared after him. Foster brother Arnbjørn Jonson was a member of King Håkon Håkonson, and was one of the foremost and most trusted loaves and h
2 CONC is armies. However, Andres took the most tenest of Arnbjørn, and was badly wounded in the battle against the slit tongues of Tunsberg in February 1218, and was soon to linger. Before he did, he sent a letter of membership with a r
2 CONC iddle to Skule Earl. The zone of Andres and Gudrun entered Gregorius Andreson the elder. He was an heir to the Stårheimsgodset, after Nicholas Arneson, and was a wrapping and governor under King Håkon Håkonson (1217-1263).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' The old Samband Stårheim – Orre at Jæren in the middle age - https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Ættesambandet_Stårheim_–_Orre_på_Jæren_i_mellomalderen
2 CONT
