1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Knut Jonsson (Aspenäs)==
2 CONT
2 CONT *Son of Johan Filipsson(Aspenäs) and Ingeborg Svantepolksdotter 
2 CONT * Knut Jonsson(son of Johan Filipsson, tab. 2). Mentioned for the first time in 1292. Not yet a knight in 1298. Was a knight and councilor 1305, a layman in Östergötland 1310 and King Birger was killed in 1311 and another 1314. Le
2 CONC ft around the turn of the year 1314-1315. Mentioned again as a layman in Östergötland in 1315 and still in 1316, but in 1318 his brother-in-law Bo Nilsson (Natt og Dag) is the layman there. Is again murdered in 1322 and yet again 
2 CONC in 1333, as well as the lawman in Östergötland in 1330 and again in 1345. Was formerly killed in 1334. Appears last time 25.9 1345, when he and his wife renew their will. Was dead 18.3 1347. Several of Mr. Knut's 1343 and 1345 let
2 CONC ters issued as dating site Aspenäs in Malexanders sn in Ydre hd in Östergötl., Where at least his wife is reported to have been resident. Was 5.6 1319 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married to '''Katarina Bengtsdotter,''' daughter of the East Gothic man the knight Bengt Magnusson (Folkungaättens teamman branch) and his wife Sigrid. Mrs Katarina issued a letter with Aspenäs as a date of residence another 12.
2 CONC 3 1350, when she left her farm Rönnäs, located either in Asby snow in Ydre hd in Östergötland or in Agunnaryds snow in Sunnerbo hd in Småland. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003168965773&photo_
2 CONC id=6000000115193841837&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Filip Knutsson''' Appointed 8.1 1328 by Pope John XXII to canon in Uppsala with expectancy on probation, even though he already had a canonical and probation in Linköping. Died before November 28, 1335.
2 CONT * '''Birger Knutsson''' Named as living 1342 –12.3 1350
2 CONT * '''Magnus Knutsson,''' 1335–1366, however, troll. sistn. year knight teamman. See loss. 4th
2 CONT * '''Jon Knutsson,''' 1335—1357, knight, governor. See loss. 5th
2 CONT * '''Cecilia Knutsdotter''' Lived 12.3 1350. Was married to the knight and the National Council Bo Nilsson ( Night and Day ), who probably died in 1322. With this she was already married 16.5 1306. Called himself widow after him 2
2 CONC 5.3 1336 and still lived 18.11 1347. Mrs. Cecilia owned land in Bråbo and Ydre hd in Östergötland.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg''' Was still living on January 31, 1333, when she, as a widow of her father, was lodged in St. Klara monastery. Was married to the knight and the national council Erik Valdemarsson ( Folkungaätten ), born 1271 or 127
2 CONC 2, died 1330.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Aspen%C3%A4s%C3%A4tten
2 CONT
