1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.nb.no/items/e4c1868422e6e51ea5fa87ac3cc8ccaa?page=471 "Bakke bygdebok"] suggests that a Knut Larsen Sira mentioned in the [https://www.nb.no/items/e4c1868422e6e51ea5fa87ac3cc8ccaa?page=469 tax records 
2 CONC of 1625], and in "Koppskatten" of 1645, and son of Lars Sjursen Sira-Nedre, may have been the same person as the Knut Larsen Sira that in 1591 signed the authorization of participants from Bakke to attend the "kongehylling" of kin
2 CONC g Christian IV at Oslo 08-06-1591. It also states that the latter is mentioned at Sira-Øvre in the tax records of 1635/1636 and in the 1664 Manntall. Yet, there are some problems with the time-line. According to the 1664 Manntall,
2 CONC  the Knut Larsen Sira mentioned there was 70 years old at the time, thus born about 1594. But obviously, it is rather unlikely that he then could have signed the authorization in 1591. That Knut Larsen Sira must have been at least
2 CONC  25 years old, and probably older, at the time to have been given such a prominent assignment. Thus, that Knut Larsen Sira must have been born before 1566. Furthermore, "Bakke bygdebok" states that Knut Larsen Sira was charged, an
2 CONC d fined, for an extramarital affair in 1617; a fine that was paid for him by his mother Madelinne. It seems unlikely that a man at the age of more than 51 years would have to have his mother pay a fine on his behalf. And it seems 
2 CONC unlikely that the Knut Larsen Sira mentioned in 1591 could have been the same person as the Knut Larsen Sira mentioned in the 1664 Manntall, at which time he would have been at least 98 years old. '''It thus seems likely that ther
2 CONC e must have been at least two persons named Knut Larsen Sira at the time'''. The Knut Larsen Sira that was the father of Lars Knutsen Hellesmark (Sira); Østen Knutsen Sira? (Konstali); and Torkel Knutsen Sira-Øvre (Audeland); Stål
2 CONC e Knutsen Brikland (Sira) must have been the older of them, i.e. "Knut I Larsen Sira", the one listed in 1591. It seems likely that the one listed in "Koppskatten" of 1645 and the 1664 Manntall was a different person, Knut II Lars
2 CONC en Sira, and he was actually an age-mate of the children of "Knut I Larsen Sira". "Knut I Larsen Sira" was thus not a son of Lars Sjursen Sira-Nedre and Madelaine (Sira-Nedre). Nor could "Knut I Larsen Sira" have been married to a
2 CONC  daughter of Sigbjørn Tollaksen Stordrange; she was too young to have fathered his children; but she may well have been married to "Knut II Larsen Sira".
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rogaland fylke, Jæren og Dalane, Skiftekort (1672-1693), Skifteprotokollside, Side 93 Brukslenke for sidevisning: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/sk20110328650233 '''[This is the probate of a completely different person, namely [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/people/Knut-Ovedal-Konstali/6000000011706897242 Knut Håversen Ovedal/ Konstali (Lindland)].'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
