2 CONT j. Ingeri, b. 1650, m. Johannes Torsteinson Hausken, farmer at Hausken in Hjelmeland.
2 CONT k. Hadle, b. 1656, farmer at Hamra in Erfjord. See Erfjordboka p. 131.
2 CONT Lars Asgautson died in the period 1658-1661. Widow Bergitte married around 1665 m. Torbjørn Johannesson Hausken. At that time, the then vicar of Nedstrand, Peder Hiermann, Jørstad. He had bought the farm from Royal Commissioner Ha
2 CONC ns Lilienskiold who probably sold it on behalf of the Cathedral in Bergen.
2 CONT Jørstad was at that time divided into two uses, upper and lower. Quarter of 1 1/2 laup and 18 mrk. butter - or 1 laup, 2 bpd. and 6 mrk. The lower yard, which was the original yard, was taken over by Lars Larsson, son of Lars Asga
2 CONC utson from his first marriage. This mill received 1st no. 38, later 175. From 1886 br. no. 1. Torbjørn and Bergitte moved into the new yard in Øvre garden. This mill received 1st no. 39, later 176. From 1886 br. no. 3. (The former
2 CONC  homestead Vågen was divided into Nedre farm in 1882 and entered as farm no. 2.)
2 CONT To begin with, Lars and Torbjørn lived as tenants under the Nedstrandpriest. But by deed of 27 June 1692 they were allowed to buy the farms from Mrs. Inger Simonsdatter, the widow of Mr. Peder.
