2 CONC n 11. des. 1732 tgl. skjøte på 12 3/5 mrk. smør i Jørstad-arven hennar Siri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Larsson had 2 horses, 20 cattle and 40 sheep. Then he sowed 5 barrels of grain and harvested 50 barrels. None of the children after Lars lived in Jørstad after him. It was his son Lars Larsson from Elfarvik who became a farme
2 CONC r in Nedre Jørstad after his grandfather. He got on 14 Dec. 1729 deed of 1 bpd. 11/5 pm. butter in Jørstad from his father in Elfarvik and just as much from his uncle Stein, who then lived in Skartveit. From his paternal sister-hu
2 CONC sband Johannes Toreson Eide, he had 11 Dec. 1732 deed of 12 3/5 mrk. butter in Siri's Jørstad heritage.
